// _prove_pilot2 -- proof pilot for quantile.mbt::array_min/array_max.
//
// This is a parallel package to _prove_pilot (which targets kfold.mbt).
// Pilot 2 tests the hypothesis: the `Array[T] -> array` Why3 lowering
// gap identified in Pilot 1 is global (any function whose signature
// touches `Array[T]` fails), not just scoped to struct fields. The
// test is to apply the same leaf-function contract pattern to
// `quantile.mbt::array_min` (a 10-line helper with no struct fields
// and a single `Array[Double]` parameter) and observe whether the
// gap fires. The gap DOES fire -- see QUANTILE_HANDOFF.md for the
// reproduction.
//
// To demonstrate that the gap is specifically about `Array[T]`
// (rather than the function shape, the loop, or the `<` operator),
// this package contains a `FixedArray[Double]` mirror of
// `array_min` / `array_max` (`array_min_view` / `array_max_view`).
// The mirror uses the same algorithm shape but with `FixedArray`,
// which the proof pipeline can reason about. If `moon prove` on
// this package succeeds, it proves that the gap is exactly
// `Array[T]` and that the migration strategy is:
//   1. Either refactor the main package's `Array[T]` to
//      `FixedArray[T]` in the surface we want to verify
//      (intrusive but the cleanest path)
//   2. Or push the proof target into a separate mirror package
//      and reason about the math at the FixedArray level
//      (non-intrusive; what `_prove_pilot` and this package do)
//   3. Or fix the moon prove toolchain so `Array[T]` operations
//      are lowered correctly (file upstream)
options(
  "proof-enabled": true,
)
